# Rebuild after changes

After any change that affects what the user sees in the app (`ui/`, `source/`, `CMakeLists.txt`, or plugin-related CMake), **rebuild every shipping format** and report success or errors. Do not ask the user to rebuild manually unless the toolchain is broken.

## Required build

Prefer the full default build:

```bash
cmake --build Builds
```

That rebuilds Standalone, AU, VST3, AUv3, and CLAP, refreshes `assets/webview/ui.zip` in BinaryData when `ui/` changed, and copies built plugins to `~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/` when `COPY_PLUGIN_AFTER_BUILD` is on.

Do not build only the standalone app unless the user explicitly asks for that narrow target; DAW plugin bundles can otherwise remain stale.

## WebView UI (`ui/`)

Editors load the UI from **`assets/webview/ui.zip` embedded in BinaryData**, not from `ui/dist` directly.

Svelte 5 sources in `ui/` must pass:

```bash
cd ui && npm run check
```

Then run the full CMake build so every binary embeds the new zip:

```bash
cmake --build Builds
```

`npm run dev` alone does not update standalone or plugin binaries. Debug builds load `http://localhost:5173` only while that Vite server is running.

Built standalone app (Debug):

`Builds/KSH_artefacts/Debug/Standalone/KSH.app`

After rebuilding the standalone, fully quit and reopen it. Relaunching an already-running instance can keep the old embedded UI.

## Plugin C++ (`source/`), CMake, tests

1. If `CMakeLists.txt` changed: `cmake -B Builds -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug`
2. Always: `cmake --build Builds`
3. Run `./Builds/Tests` when test or processor behavior changes.

## DAW reload

After plugin binaries change, remove the plugin instance and reopen it, or restart the DAW. Rescan plug-in folders only when the host does not pick up replaced bundles automatically.
